evidence:
POC execution results confirm protocol validation bypass:

Test Results:
- Gopher protocol (gopher://127.0.0.1:4455/) - ACCEPTED
- FTP protocol (ftp://internal-ftp:4455/) - ACCEPTED  
- Dict protocol (dict://redis-server:4455/) - ACCEPTED
- LDAP protocol (ldap://ldap-server:4455/) - ACCEPTED
- PHP wrapper protocol (php://filter/...) - ACCEPTED

The POC script tests multiple dangerous protocols and demonstrates that filter_var() does not validate or restrict the protocol scheme. All tested non-HTTP protocols were accepted by the endpoint, confirming the vulnerability.

Vulnerable code from sku_url.php:
```php
if (filter_var($url, FILTER_VALIDATE_URL) === FALSE) {
    return 'Invalid URL';
}
$urlComponents = parse_url($url);
// No protocol/scheme validation
$response = file_get_contents($url, false, $context);
```

The code comment claims "HTTP/HTTPS URLs" but contains no enforcement of this requirement.

remediation:
1. ADD EXPLICIT PROTOCOL VALIDATION:
```php
public function fetchSkuModel($url) {
    // Validate URL format
    if (filter_var($url, FILTER_VALIDATE_URL) === FALSE) {
        return 'Invalid URL';
    }

    // Parse URL components
    $urlComponents = parse_url($url);

    // CRITICAL: Whitelist allowed schemes (HTTP/HTTPS only)
    $scheme = $urlComponents['scheme'] ?? '';
    if (!in_array($scheme, ['http', 'https'], true)) {
        return 'Invalid protocol. Only HTTP/HTTPS allowed.';
    }

    // Continue with rest of validation...
}
```

2. DISABLE DANGEROUS STREAM WRAPPERS (php.ini):
```ini
# Disable potentially dangerous URL wrappers
allow_url_fopen = Off
# Or if you need URL fopen, at least disable dangerous wrappers
```

3. USE A SAFE HTTP CLIENT LIBRARY (RECOMMENDED):
```php
use GuzzleHttp\Client;

$client = new Client([
    'allow_redirects' => false,
    'timeout' => 10,
    'verify' => true,  // SSL verification
]);

try {
    $response = $client->request('GET', $url);
    return $response->getBody();
} catch (Exception $e) {
    return 'Failed to fetch URL';
}
```

4. COMPREHENSIVE FIX WITH MULTIPLE VALIDATIONS:
```php
public function fetchSkuModel($url) {
    // 1. Basic URL format validation
    if (filter_var($url, FILTER_VALIDATE_URL) === FALSE) {
        return 'Invalid URL';
    }

    // 2. Parse URL components
    $urlComponents = parse_url($url);

    // 3. Validate scheme (HTTP/HTTPS only) - CRITICAL
    $scheme = $urlComponents['scheme'] ?? '';
    if (!in_array($scheme, ['http', 'https'], true)) {
        return 'Invalid protocol. Only HTTP/HTTPS allowed.';
    }

    // 4. Validate port (must be 4455)
    if (!isset($urlComponents['port']) || $urlComponents['port'] != 4455) {
        return 'Invalid port. Only port 4455 allowed.';
    }

    // 5. Whitelist allowed hosts
    $host = $urlComponents['host'] ?? '';
    $allowedHosts = ['skumodel', 'localhost', '127.0.0.1'];
    if (!in_array($host, $allowedHosts, true)) {
        return 'Invalid host. Only skumodel is allowed.';
    }

    // 6. Build safe URL with all components normalized
    $url = $scheme . '://' . $host . ':' . $urlComponents['port'];
    if (isset($urlComponents['path'])) {
        $url .= $urlComponents['path'];
    }

    // Now safe to use with file_get_contents
    return $this->safeFileGetContents($url);
}
```
